    "problem_statement": "QR code generation produces incorrect version numbers\n\nWhen generating QR codes, the library is selecting higher version numbers than necessary, causing inefficient encoding. This affects both optimized and non-optimized data encoding.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\nfrom qrcode.constants import MODE_ALPHA_NUM, MODE_NUMBER\n\n# Test alphanumeric mode\nqr = qrcode.QRCode()\nqr.add_data('ABCDEFGHIJ1234567890', optimize=0)\nqr.make()\nprint(f\"Expected version: 1, Got version: {qr.version}\")\n\n# Test numeric mode  \nqr = qrcode.QRCode()\nqr.add_data('1234567890123456789012345678901234', optimize=0)\nqr.make()\nprint(f\"Expected version: 1, Got version: {qr.version}\")\n\n# Test optimization\nqr = qrcode.QRCode()\ntext = 'A1abc12345def1HELLOa'\nqr.add_data(text, optimize=4)\nqr.make()\nprint(f\"Expected version: 2, Got version: {qr.version}\")\n```\n\nThe code above should produce version 1 QR codes for the first two examples and version 2 for the optimized example, but instead produces higher version numbers, resulting in unnecessarily large QR codes."
